    "body": "> > \"get in touch and ask for a data-export attribute if you think you need to reference one of these terms\"\r\n\r\nFWIW if this were the case I'd be much more likely to simply link to the spec section instead, as a \"workaround\". That is, instead of `[=serializable object=]`, I'd write `[[HTML#serializable-objects|serializable object]]`.\r\n\r\nActually, in this case, that's the only thing you can link to - the `dfn` doesn't _have_ an ID, only the section does. So that's exactly what I'm going to do to fix the WebGPU spec build, at least for now.\r\n\r\nI'm guessing Shepherd must have had some special logic to treat this pattern as both a section and a dfn? Since there's only one URL for both.",
