    "updated_at": "2023-01-18T21:53:15Z",
    "body": "It's always an option to work around (e.g., using manual `<a>`) instead of improve the spec ecosystem definition database for everyone. But, I hope most people will chose to do the latter. It's certainly been the case in the past.\r\n\r\nAs for the markup, indeed, we need two things here:\r\n\r\n- HTML needs to add `export`, and maybe `data-lt=\"serializable object\"` to depluralize, to the source `<dfn>`.\r\n- Webref needs to recognize HTML's unusual pattern of having `id`-less `<dfn>`s inside of `id`-having `<hN>`s as part of its database-building logic. (I think this is worth doing, instead of having HTML add an id to the definition, as HTML's pattern is unusual but logical: having two IDs for basically the same thing just causes confusion.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
