    "updated_at": "2023-01-18T23:02:14Z",
    "body": "It's such a small workaround though, that it doesn't really feel like I'm doing something wrong. Note, Bikeshed now validates `[[spec#section]]` links are valid and link to actual sections; I just fixed up a bunch of links of that style in WebGPU/WGSL that were being used to point to non-section things.\r\n\r\n> * (I think this is worth doing, instead of having HTML add an id to the definition, as HTML's pattern is unusual but logical: having two IDs for basically the same thing just causes confusion.)\r\n\r\nWebGPU has run into this, but unfortunately I don't think Bikeshed can do this pattern. It always generates `id`s for `dfn`s, but also wants `id`s for headings, so we either have 2 `id`s or a duplicate `id`.",
