    "created_at": "2023-01-19T09:36:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-19T09:36:32Z",
    "body": "> Webref needs to recognize HTML's unusual pattern of having id-less <dfn>s inside of id-having <hN>s as part of its database-building logic. (I think this is worth doing, instead of having HTML add an id to the definition, as HTML's pattern is unusual but logical: having two IDs for basically the same thing just causes confusion.)\r\n\r\nI confirm that Webref has that logic already. It just failed to take the `data-export` and `data-lt` attributes on the heading into account (used in \"Transferable objects\" heading). Crawler fixed yesterday in https://github.com/w3c/reffy/pull/1183, and Webref now reports \"transferable object\" as a public term.\r\n\r\nThe definition of \"serializable object\" is not yet marked up as exported in the HTML spec, so it's still extracted as a private term for now.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
