    "created_at": "2023-01-20T19:24:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-20T19:24:39Z",
    "body": "> WebGPU has run into this, but unfortunately I don't think Bikeshed can do this pattern. It always generates ids for dfns, but also wants ids for headings, so we either have 2 ids or a duplicate id.\r\n\r\nNote that Bikeshed has a *different* pattern to handle that - you can put all the `dfn-*` attributes on headings, and they'll serve as a definition source as well. (This is documented in the [Dfn contract](https://tabatkins.github.io/bikeshed/#dfn-contract).)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
